00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:46.780
[George] Hi Mr. O'Leary

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:52.040
My name is George Romero and thank you for taking the time to answer my question. Here it is

00:08:52.700 --> 00:09:00.180
Are there any circumstances in which you would advise an entrepreneur not to make a deal with a Shark?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.680
Thank you so much.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:05.300
[Kevin]  Wow, interesting.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.320
[Robert] Because they actually want to get their money.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:19.090
[Kevin] You know, I've never had that question before but I'll tell you how I'm gonna answer it.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:23.020
I think you have to think about which Shark you want to work with.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.360
Well I think it provides a very important platform in America...

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.500
that

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:33.620
lets consumers discover new products and services

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.060
and

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.840
the trends...

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:43.220
Shark Tank is probably at the cutting edge of what's happening out there

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:51.320
There's constant innovation. There's constant new ideas. Some of which have no merit but many are amazing

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.850
and so...

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:58.220
Then it's up to the investors to decide which of which is which and take a chance on them. They don't all work out

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.400
but when they work

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.420
it's pretty phenomenal.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:03.040
Because

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:08.320
Shark Tanks been on for 11 years. It's in it's 11th season, so everybody knows every Shark now.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:14.890
I know it get's guest Sharks once in a while, but the Sharks that have been there for over a decade. Mr. Wonderful included

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:19.569
I might add, you've gotten to know by now and I would do two things

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:26.710
If the deal makes no sense, obviously, you don't feel like it's fair. Obviously you don't do that deal. I like royalty deals

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:32.889
I like venture debt. I like, you know, all kinds of different structures because I'm the financial Shark, but I always let...

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:40.179
you know entrepreneurs talk to the rest of my company's CEOs and men and women that manage all the different

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:44.979
you know companies that I've invested in. They're my best...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:45.620
I think

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:51.130
people to provide due diligence and what it's really like to work with. Mr. Wonderful and I come up with some pretty good grades

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.439
I'm happy to say. They're my best salesmen.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:57.939
I mean all of my CEOs are my best salesmen, we gather every year but to actually

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:01.599
not work with a Shark is it's because you've determined that

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:04.660
they don't add a lot of value other than money to your situation.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:09.219
The reason you want to come into the Shark world is that Shark can help you significantly

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:14.500
reduce your customer acquisition cost by getting you out on their massive social platform.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.740
I've got millions of followers

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:21.820
obviously and I love all my companies and you constantly see me putting them out on social media to tell people about the new products

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:22.780
and services, that's what I do

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.989
that's how I add value and of course, I'd love to give mentorship and I provide capital

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.899
I do all that and I have a great team of people working with me.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:35.860
But the reason you wouldn't invest with the Shark is you don't think there's a fit. It's that simple.

